    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.09",
    "order": 203,
    "anchor": "15.09",
    "summary": "Snap Shooting is used only when another rule allows it. The unit shoots following [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks), with these limits:\n\n- It picks only one eligible enemy unit within 24″ that it can [see](vsdata:core-rule/visibility); each weapon's choice still uses the [attacking model's view](vsdata:core-rule/select-targets).\n- Only a natural 6 hits, whatever the Ballistic Skill or modifiers, and those hits never count as **Critical Hits**.\n- **Hit rolls** cannot be re-rolled.\n\nUntil the phase ends, the unit cannot **start an Action**.",
